{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "25890036",
      "title": "Understanding Different Kinds Of Tests",
      "sourceHash": "5b606bd93bd2595fd53e96b6b05966b6d7ba019274f2d15be5c25caaab8944b6",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.35,
          "end": 5.47,
          "en": "Now, when we speak about automated testing,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 5.47,
          "end": 9.14,
          "en": "it is important to understand that there are different kinds",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 9.14,
          "end": 12.78,
          "en": "of automated tests which you can have a look at.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 12.78,
          "end": 16.82,
          "en": "For example, there are unit tests and I can already say",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 16.82,
          "end": 19.7,
          "en": "that those will be super important.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 19.7,
          "end": 22.64,
          "en": "But you also have so-called integration tests",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 22.64,
          "end": 25.23,
          "en": "and end to end tests.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 25.23,
          "end": 29.06,
          "en": "Now, these are the three main categories of tests",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 29.06,
          "end": 30.48,
          "en": "which you can write.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 30.48,
          "end": 34.5,
          "en": "Unit tests are all about writing tests",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 34.5,
          "end": 38.64,
          "en": "for the smallest possible units off your application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 38.64,
          "end": 42.89,
          "en": "So for functions, individual functions that you use",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 42.89,
          "end": 44.31,
          "en": "in your application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 44.31,
          "end": 46.67,
          "en": "Or in case of React apps,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 46.67,
          "end": 49.95,
          "en": "testing some components independently",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 49.95,
          "end": 52.97,
          "en": "from the other components in your app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 52.97,
          "end": 56.2,
          "en": "And therefore projects typically contain a lot",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 56.2,
          "end": 59.76,
          "en": "of unit tests, since you basically wanna test",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 59.76,
          "end": 63.4,
          "en": "all the units, all the functions and components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 63.4,
          "end": 65.93,
          "en": "that make up your application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 65.93,
          "end": 68.37,
          "en": "And hence this is the most common",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 68.37,
          "end": 71.06,
          "en": "and important kind of test.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 71.06,
          "end": 72.72,
          "en": "And the idea simply is that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 72.72,
          "end": 76.14,
          "en": "if you test all the individual units on themselves,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 76.14,
          "end": 78.623,
          "en": "the overall application will also work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 79.48,
          "end": 84.05,
          "en": "But to verify that the overall application really works",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 84.05,
          "end": 86.5,
          "en": "if you put together all those units,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 86.5,
          "end": 88.86,
          "en": "we have integration tests.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 88.86,
          "end": 93.25999999999999,
          "en": "Here, we test the combination of multiple building blocks.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 93.25999999999999,
          "end": 96.443,
          "en": "For example, multiple components working together.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 97.65,
          "end": 99.78,
          "en": "And projects typically contain",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 99.78,
          "end": 102.35,
          "en": "a couple of such integration tests,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 102.35,
          "end": 105.7,
          "en": "but not as many as you have unit tests.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 105.7,
          "end": 109.78999999999999,
          "en": "Though as you will also see throughout this course section,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 109.78999999999999,
          "end": 113.02000000000001,
          "en": "it's not always that easy to differentiate",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 114.138,
          "end": 117.22999999999999,
          "en": "between unit and integration tests when testing React apps,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 117.22999999999999,
          "end": 120.21,
          "en": "since very often, you wanna test a component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 120.21,
          "end": 123.43,
          "en": "that also uses some other component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 123.43,
          "end": 125.96,
          "en": "But we're going to see that in action",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 125.96,
          "end": 127.93,
          "en": "throughout this course section.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 127.93,
          "end": 132.01,
          "en": "So generally, integration tests are also extremely important",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 132.01,
          "end": 137.01,
          "en": "but we have fewer integration tests than we have unit tests.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 137.4,
          "end": 140.6,
          "en": "And then we also have end to end tests.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 140.6,
          "end": 145.6,
          "en": "These are all about testing entire workflows",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 145.87,
          "end": 147.68,
          "en": "in your application, you could say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 147.68,
          "end": 151.57,
          "en": "Entire scenarios, like logging a user in",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 151.57,
          "end": 154.35,
          "en": "and then going to a certain page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 154.35,
          "end": 159.35,
          "en": "So these aim to really reproduce what a real human would do",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 159.88,
          "end": 161.6,
          "en": "with your website.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 161.6,
          "end": 164.95,
          "en": "Basically what you would also do with manual testing,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 164.95,
          "end": 166.71,
          "en": "just automated.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 166.71,
          "end": 170.57999999999998,
          "en": "Now, whilst this might sound like the most important test",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 170.57999999999998,
          "end": 172.16,
          "en": "it definitely is important",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 172.16,
          "end": 175.44,
          "en": "and you therefore typically do write some end to end tests",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 175.44,
          "end": 178.77,
          "en": "but not as many as you have unit and integration tests,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 178.77,
          "end": 181.72,
          "en": "because if your a unit and integration tests work,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 181.72,
          "end": 186.13,
          "en": "you can be pretty sure that your overall application works.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 186.13,
          "end": 188.97,
          "en": "And then those unit and integration tests",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 188.97,
          "end": 191.81,
          "en": "are simply easier to test.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 191.81,
          "end": 196.52,
          "en": "They often are quicker to run and they are more focused",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 196.52,
          "end": 199.85,
          "en": "and it's way easier to test all possible scenarios,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 199.85,
          "end": 203.47,
          "en": "if you test all your units for different scenarios",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 203.47,
          "end": 206.64,
          "en": "then coming up with all possible scenarios,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 206.64,
          "end": 208.88,
          "en": "if you look at your app as a whole,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 208.88,
          "end": 212.84,
          "en": "which is what you do typically with end to end tests.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 212.84,
          "end": 214.85,
          "en": "So these are important,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 214.85,
          "end": 217.59,
          "en": "but it's basically all to what you do manually",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 217.59,
          "end": 221.52,
          "en": "and therefore you have fewer of those tests.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 221.52,
          "end": 224.7,
          "en": "Now in this course section, since it's an introduction",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 224.7,
          "end": 225.55,
          "en": "to testing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 225.55,
          "end": 228.35,
          "en": "We will focus on those most important kinds",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 228.35,
          "end": 229.24,
          "en": "of tests.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 229.24,
          "end": 233.74,
          "en": "Unit tests and also to some extent integration tests.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 233.74,
          "end": 236.76,
          "en": "But at the end of the module, I will also point you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 236.76,
          "end": 239.65,
          "en": "at some other resources, which you can check out",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 239.65,
          "end": 242.943,
          "en": "to dive deeper into React testing if you want to.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}